{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Constraint from the model-upgrade audit (beaten-natural-grouse, 2026-11-09): Bedrock Opus 5.5 declines (content_filtered) requests whose prompt or output schema ask for the reasoning to be written into the response, e.g. a field described 'Scratchpad — reason before emitting.' or 'REASON FIRST: ...'. Measured on the plan-review and code-review contracts; neutral wording fixes it. The adapted agentic prompt and its findings schema must not ask for reasoning in the output (the agent reasons in thinking blocks); tests/unit/test_output_contract_no_reasoning_in_output.py scans every registered contract and will catch the new schema. Also handle a declined run as INDETERMINATE (the epic's fail-closed invariant covers refusal/content_filter)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794269556070944001,"uuid":"2c778328-4b46-4b07-a3a2-22325ae58f83"}